# tests/pins/tinycc.sha256 -- sha256 of what the route builds that
# live-bootstrap does not publish.  Paths are relative to build-out/.
#   tinycc/tcc-first-i386
#                      build-out/tinycc/tcc-first-i386, the first tcc:
#                      janneke's tcc-0.9.26 with Mes libc, compiled by the
#                      seed (tinycc/build-first-tcc-i386.sh, 975,624
#                      bytes); /usr/bin/tcc-mes in the boot.  The same in
#                      two checkouts at different paths.
#   tinycc/junction/usr/bin/tcc-boot0
#                      what the first tcc makes of tcc.c in
#                      live-bootstrap's pass1.kaem
#                      (tests/tinycc/junction-check.sh, and the boot).
#                      MesCC's tcc-mes makes ea464b2f...; from boot1 on the
#                      two routes have the same bytes.  It equals what a
#                      gcc -m32 build of the first tcc makes
#                      (tests/tinycc/i386-standin-check.sh).
#   tinycc/bin-i386/*  build-out/tinycc/bin-i386/, the source preparation
#                      tools the seed builds against M2libc
#                      (tinycc/build-tools-i386.sh)
#   tinycc/bin-boot-i386/*
#                      build-out/tinycc/bin-boot-i386/, ungz and untar from
#                      stage0-posix's sources as published; the route
#                      unpacks live-bootstrap's archive with them once
#   tinycc/kaem-i386   build-out/tinycc/kaem-i386, vendor/mescc-tools/Kaem
#                      compiled like those tools, with the process calls
#                      of tinycc/m2libc-kaem-i386.c (99,008 bytes).
#   tinycc/first/...
#                      what tcc-mes makes in the one boot before the later
#                      stages overwrite it (the boot keeps copies under
#                      /first): the mes libc (all but libc.a equal what
#                      live-bootstrap publishes after tcc-boot2) and
#                      hex0-export, which it builds against that libc
#                      (tests/tinycc/i386-one-boot-check.sh).
# When a change is meant to alter one, update its line in the same commit
# and say why.
